Usage: vcpe down [flags]

Stops compose services, removes their protected wireless credential files, and releases all IPAM leases for the named deployment. Credentials are removed only after consumers stop. Alias: destroy (destroy also requires --force).

Optional flags:
  --name <deployment>     Name of the deployment to tear down (metadata.name from the manifest)
  --manifest <path>       Path to the manifest file; metadata.name is used as the deployment name
  --state-root <path>     Override the default state root directory
  --socket <path>         Override the daemon socket path

Examples:
  vcpe down --name bng-7
  vcpe down --manifest manifests/example.yaml
